.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt NQDADDR 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqdaddr ,
.Nm nqdvrfy ,
.Nm nqdfld ,
.Nm nqdrslv ,
.Nm nqdrsp ,
.Nm nqdwb
.Nd where a source can be fetched from, the check of what was fetched, and portal resolvers
.Sh LIBRARY
libnqd, \-lnqd \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In nqd.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqdaddr
.Fa "const nqdrec *r" "const char *path" "size_t i" "int *kind"
.Fa "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqdvrfy
.Fa "const nqdrec *r" "const char *path" "const uint8_t *b" "size_t n"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqdfld
.Fa "const nqdrec *r" "const char *member" "size_t i" "const char *field"
.Fa "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqdrslv
.Fa "const char *rslv" "size_t n" "char *out" "size_t cap"
.Fa "size_t *outlen" "char *why" "size_t wcap"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqdrsp
.Fa "const char *rslv" "size_t n" "const char *reply" "size_t rn"
.Fa "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen" "char tm[21]"
.Fa "char *why" "size_t wcap"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqdwb
.Fa "const char *url" "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions make no network request: they say what to fetch and
read what came back, and the caller moves the bytes, as
.Xr noqtis-src 1
does.
In each,
.Fa out
gets a NUL-terminated text of at most
.Fa cap
bytes and
.Fa *outlen
its length, also when
.Fa cap
is too small
.Pq Dv NQEBUF ,
as for
.Xr nqdjson 3 .
.Pp
.Fn nqdaddr
gives address
.Fa i
(0, 1, ...) from which the source
.Fa path
of the record
.Fa r
.Pq the Ql sources No member of Xr noqtis-data 5
can be fetched, in the order to try them, and in
.Fa *kind
(which may be
.Dv NULL )
where it comes from:
.Bl -tag -width "NQDAPORT"
.It Dv NQDAURL
the source's
.Cm url ,
then the
.Cm base
of a
.Ql direct
resolver when it differs;
.It Dv NQDAPORT
the portal of its
.Cm resolver :
the address is the request of
.Fn nqdrslv ,
whose reply
.Fn nqdrsp
reads;
.It Dv NQDAMIR
each of its
.Cm mirrors ,
in order;
.It Dv NQDAARC
its
.Cm archived
copy, a Wayback Machine copy in the raw form of
.Fn nqdwb .
.El
.Pp
Whatever address answers, only bytes that
.Fn nqdvrfy
accepts are the file:
.Fn nqdvrfy
compares the
.Fa n
bytes at
.Fa b
with the size and SHA-256 the source records.
.Pp
.Fn nqdfld
writes the value of
.Fa field
of element
.Fa i
of
.Fa member
.Pf ( Fa i
0 for
.Ql env
and
.Ql cite ) :
a string as its text, any other value as canonical JSON.
.Pp
.Fn nqdrslv
writes the address to ask (an HTTP GET) for the resolver
.Fa rslv
.Pf ( Fa n
bytes of JSON, a source's
.Cm resolver
object), and
.Fn nqdrsp
reads the portal's JSON reply
.Pf ( Fa rn
bytes, at most 16 MiB) to it and writes the address of the file.
.Cm base
is the portal's address, http:// or https://, without a query; trailing
slashes are dropped.
Each kind:
.Bl -tag -width "socrata"
.It Ql ckan
with
.Cm id
(a dataset's name or id):
.Ql <base>/api/3/action/package_show?id=<id> ;
the reply must be a
.Cm success
whose
.Cm result
lists
.Cm resources :
the one whose
.Cm id ,
else whose
.Cm name ,
is
.Cm resource
when it is given, else the first whose
.Cm format
is
.Cm format
(default CSV, in any case).
With only
.Cm resource
(a resource's id):
.Ql <base>/api/3/action/resource_show?id=<resource> ,
whose
.Cm result
is that resource.
The file is the resource's
.Cm url .
.It Ql socrata
with
.Cm id ,
the four-by-four id (such as
.Ql abcd-1234 ) :
.Ql <base>/api/views/<id>.json ;
the reply must be that dataset's metadata (its
.Cm id ) ,
and the file is
.Ql <base>/api/views/<id>/rows.csv?accessType=DOWNLOAD
.Pf ( Cm format
.Ql json :
.Ql rows.json ) .
.It Ql arcgis
with
.Cm id ,
an item id (32 hex digits), of a portal such as
.Ql https://www.arcgis.com :
.Ql <base>/sharing/rest/content/items/<id>?f=json ;
the reply must be that item: a
.Ql Feature Service
or
.Ql Map Service
gives the query of every feature of its layer
.Cm layer
(default 0),
.Ql <url>/<layer>/query?where=1%3D1&outFields=*&f=geojson
.Pf ( Cm format
.Ql json :
.Ql f=json ) ;
any other item (a CSV file, a spreadsheet) gives its data,
.Ql <base>/sharing/rest/content/items/<id>/data .
Without
.Cm id ,
.Cm base
is a FeatureServer or MapServer:
.Ql <base>/<layer>?f=json ,
whose reply must be the layer's metadata (a
.Cm name ,
no
.Cm error ) ,
and the file is that layer's query.
A server returns at most its
.Cm maxRecordCount
features to one query.
.It Ql wayback
with
.Cm base ,
the archived address, and optionally
.Cm id ,
a time of 1 to 14 digits
.Pq Ql YYYYMMDDhhmmss No or a prefix of it :
.Ql https://archive.org/wayback/available?url=<base>[&timestamp=<id>] ;
the reply's
.Cm archived_snapshots.closest
must be
.Cm available ,
of an HTTP 200 answer, with a valid
.Cm timestamp ,
and the file is that copy's raw bytes,
.Ql https://web.archive.org/web/<timestamp>id_/<base> ,
built here: the reply's own address is not followed.
.Fa tm
(which may be
.Dv NULL )
gets the copy's time,
.Ql YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ ,
for the source's
.Cm archived
member; it is empty for the other kinds.
.El
.Pp
Values put in a query are percent-encoded but for the unreserved bytes
of RFC 3986.
An address read from a reply must be http:// or https://, at most 4,096
bytes, without a space, control character, backslash or fragment, and
https:// when the portal is.
.Pp
.Fn nqdwb
writes the address of the raw bytes of a Wayback Machine copy,
.Ql https://web.archive.org/web/<time>id_/<address> ,
for the address of one of its copies,
.Ql web.archive.org/web/<time>[<modifier>]/<address> ;
any other http:// or https:// address is written as it is.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK
on success;
.Dv NQEBUF
for a
.Fa cap
too small.
.Fn nqdaddr :
.Dv NQEIO
when the record has no source
.Fa path
or it has no address
.Fa i ;
.Dv NQEARG
for a source marked
.Cm synthetic ,
which has none.
.Fn nqdvrfy :
.Dv NQEVRFY
when the bytes are not those recorded;
.Dv NQEIO
when there is no source
.Fa path .
.Fn nqdfld :
.Dv NQEIO
when there is no such element or field.
.Fn nqdrslv
and
.Fn nqdrsp :
.Dv NQEARG ,
with a sentence in
.Fa why
.Pf ( Fa wcap
bytes, may be
.Dv NULL ) ,
for a resolver that names no request: a
.Ql direct
one, one without its
.Cm base
or
.Cm id ,
an id of the wrong form, a
.Cm format
the portal does not export there;
.Dv NQEDEC ,
with
.Fa why ,
for a resolver that is not one
.Pq Xr noqtis-data 5
or a reply that is not JSON, not the portal's answer, or names no file
or an address refused above;
.Dv NQELIM
for a reply over 16 MiB or a request over 4,096 bytes.
.Fn nqdwb :
.Dv NQEARG
for an address that is not http:// or https://, or a Wayback Machine one
without the address after its time.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-src 1 ,
.Xr nqdnew 3 ,
.Xr nqdsrc 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
